  "question": {
    "html": "<p>Source X and source Y both emit waves of wavelength 0.40 m. There is a constant phase angle of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\pi\"></span> rad between the sources. Point P is 5.2 m from X and 4.6 m from Y. The amplitude of each wave at P is A.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>What is the amplitude of the resultant wave at P?<br/><br/></p>\n<p>[1]</p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\">0</li><li data-label=\"B\">A</li><li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{3}{2}\"></span>A</li><li data-label=\"D\">2A</li></ol>"
  },
